  "description": "XOYRAF crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/n. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H88 Gd8 N12 O48 4+,4(Cl1 O4 1-),3(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Gd1 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2 (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4 (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd1B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd2B (Gd) has 7 O neighbors; Gd3B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors; Gd4B (Gd) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 12 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.764-3.913 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 102.63-109.33°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C72H88Cl4Gd8N12O64. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 8 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
